<section id="portfolio">
    <h2>My Sample Projects</h2>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Project 1: Appointment Follow-Up</h3>
        <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A potential customer has shown interest
        but has not booked a consultation.</p>

        <p><strong>Sample message:</strong></p>

        <p>
            Hello Jordan, I am following up on your recent enquiry.
            I would be happy to help you schedule a consultation.
            Would Tuesday afternoon or Thursday morning be convenient for you?
        </p>

        <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Encourage the customer to book without
        making them feel pressured.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Project 2: Appointment Confirmation</h3>
        <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A customer has booked a meeting and
        needs confirmation.</p>

        <p><strong>Sample message:</strong></p>

        <p>
            Hello Sarah, this is a friendly confirmation of your appointment
            scheduled for Thursday at 10:00 AM. Please let me know if you
            need any assistance before the meeting. Thank you!
        </p>

        <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Help customers remember their appointments
        and keep the schedule organised.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Project 3: Managing a Customer Complaint</h3>
        <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A customer is unhappy because their
        appointment needs to be rescheduled.</p>

        <p><strong>Sample response:</strong></p>

        <p>
            I understand how inconvenient a schedule change can be, and
            I apologise for the inconvenience. I would be happy to help
            arrange another suitable time. Would you prefer a morning
            or afternoon appointment?
        </p>

        <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Respond with empathy and provide a clear
        next step toward resolving the issue.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="card">
        <h3>Project 4: Daily Administrative Task Tracker</h3>

        <p><strong>Scenario:</strong> A business owner needs help tracking
        daily administrative responsibilities.</p>

        <ul>
            <li>Check and organise incoming emails.</li>
            <li>Review the calendar and confirm appointments.</li>
            <li>Update customer records and task lists.</li>
            <li>Follow up on outstanding requests.</li>
            <li>Prepare a brief end-of-day progress update.</li>
        </ul>

        <p><strong>Goal:</strong> Improve organisation and reduce missed tasks.</p>
    </div>

    <p><em>Note: These are fictional practice projects created to demonstrate
